  "text": "Category-First Brand + Product Studio / 26 Years of Client Partnership\nContact Us\nBECOME\nA CATEGORY\nOF ONE\nWe design a category you can own—then build and launch\nthe brand and flagship digital experiences to prove it.\n(SCROLL)\nBECOME\nA CATEGORY\nOF ONE\nWe design a category you can own—then build and launch\nthe brand and flagship digital experiences to prove it.\nWANDER\nJAUNT\nWebsite & Video\nInnovative website featuring 3D & webGL\nVAREX\nIMAGING\nWebsite & Video\nAward-winning website & videos\nCAPSULE\nHOUSE\nWebsite\nWeb3 website\n\nThoughtLab is a category-first\nbrand + product studio for\norganizations at pivotal growth\nmoments. We lead with end-to-end\nstrategy and execution to make\nyou impossible to ignore.\n\nAbout Us\nCapabilities\nCategory Design\n\nCategory Design is how we invent the space you can own and build the strategy, positioning, POV, narrative, and decision rules that move you into a defensible category of one.\n\nBrand Systems\n\nBrand Systems translate your positioning into a repeatable expression and usable operating system—strategy, voice, visuals, and rules your team can apply across every touchpoint without drift.\n\nDigital Experiences\n\nDigital Experiences are the Flagship experiences where your category is felt—premium websites, storytelling, and content that make your credibility unmistakable.\n\nProduct Ecosystems\n\nProduct Ecosystems are the platforms behind the promise—mobile apps, integrations, and scalable connected systems that turn your category into repeatable product behavior.\n\nLatest news\nView all\nSeptember 14,\n2026\nThe Pressure of Language\nBy\nPaul Kiernan\nWe treat dictionaries like wise tomes that have settled everything. We go to the book, open to the word, and say, there, that’s what the word means. Except that dictionaries tend to miss the fact that language is a living thing.\nMore\nSeptember 11,\n2026\nWhen Every Word Is Premium, No Word Is\nBy\nPaul Kiernan\nWords matter in marketing because we ask them to carry enormous weight. A carefully chosen word can tell someone what a company believes, what a product promises, or why any of it should matter to them.\nMore\nSeptember 9,\n2026\nYou’re Doing It Wrong: A Field Guide to Marketing’s Favorite Lie\nBy\nPaul Kiernan\nThese lists are annoying at the very least and frenzy-causing at best. But they’re too obvious. Let’s be honest, does anyone really open an English Muffin wrong? Do the English have a muffin board that traverses the world, spying through kitchen windows in early morning light, seeking muffin defilers, the breakfast deviants who need to be taught a valuable muffin lesson? I don’t think so. So, telling me that I’m opening an English muffin wrong is pointless.\nMore\nSALT\nLAKE\nCITY\n/ USA\nHEADQUARTERS\nContact\nWork with us\n+1 801 355 2696\nContact us\nFollow us\nTwitter\nInstagram\nJoin us\nApply now\nProjects22\nAbout\nCareers1\nContact\nToniqBLOG\nPrivacy Policy\nJoin our Community\n\n© 1999_2026 / ThoughtLab LLC. All rights reserved.\n\nSLCHQ / NYC / ATL / SF",
